# Pairs with NoResurrection. Reproduces production before #4445 was fixed: the
# destination refuses a late prepare only when its activation remembers
# applying the saga's terminal. A delayed shadow-forwarded prepare that arrives
# after the decision and a newer write - before the terminal, or after a
# reactivation forgot it - is bucketed with a newer stamp and served over the
# newer row.
MODULE: NoResurrectionLatePrepareActivationMemory
TARGET: NoResurrection
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the late-prepare refusal reads per-activation memory, so a late orphan serves a stale value
PERTURBS: DeliverLate

--- FIND
    /\ IF term[spCopy][s2] \/ RegistryView # "inflight" \/ Gone(spCopy)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the refusal consults the activation's terminal memory.
    /\ IF term[spCopy][s2] \/ Gone(spCopy)
--- END